---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About | Web Guy Nick"
  description="Web Guy Nick LLC builds conversion-led, high-performance websites for small businesses."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-24 prose-custom">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-white md:text-5xl">About Web Guy Nick</h1>
    <p>
      Web Guy Nick LLC is a one-person shop focused on small businesses. I build websites
      that load fast, rank well, and, the part that matters, actually bring in work.
    </p>
    <p>
      Think of me as the opposite of a big agency: no monorail-salesman promises, no rotating
      account managers, no "we'll circle back" that never circles back. Just a real person in
      Rialto, CA who answers the phone and remembers your project. It's the perfectly cromulent
      way to run a web business — and it embiggens results without the corporate mumbo-jumbo.
    </p>
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      Most small businesses get sold flashy templates, locked-in page builders, and hosting with
      surprise renewal prices. I wanted a plain-English resource: honest reviews, real numbers,
      and tools I've seen work.
    </p>
    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Straightforward fixed pricing (see <a href="/services">Services</a>).</li>
      <li>Modern static stack, fast, secure, and cheap to host.</li>
      <li>Month-to-month maintenance. Cancel whenever.</li>
      <li>Everything I ship on your domain, you own.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:info@webguynick.com">info@webguynick.com</a> or call
      <a href="tel:+19515360028">(951) 536-0028</a>. Or just
      <a href="/contact">use the form</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
